Convention\n\nAll non-source artifacts (analysis scripts, design docs, research 
notes, validation reports, scratch files) **MUST** be placed inside the 
`.agent_tasks/` directory in the project root. **NEVER** create these files in 
the repo root or alongside source code.\n\n#### Directory 
Structure\n```\n.agent_tasks/\n├── <task-slug>/            # One folder per task
or project\n│   ├── README.md           # Task description, status, and 
findings\n│   ├── analysis/           # Analysis scripts, notebooks, data 
exploration\n│   ├── docs/               # Design docs, RFCs, research notes\n│ 
└── scripts/            # Utility/validation/automation scripts\n```\n\n#### 
Rules\n1. **Create `.agent_tasks/` if it doesn\'t exist** - Agents should create
this directory when needed\n2. **Use descriptive task slugs** - Short, 
descriptive names (e.g., `elo-parameter-tuning`, `api-migration`)\n3. **Include 
README.md** - Each task folder should have a README summarizing the goal and 
current status\n4. **Separate source from artifacts** - Source code changes go 
in normal project directories; only supporting artifacts go here\n5. **Reuse 
existing folders** - If a prior task folder exists for the same topic, reuse it 
instead of creating a new one\n6. **Keep documentation updated** - Update the 
README before, during, and after work to maintain a single source of 
truth\n\n#### Agent Responsibilities\n- **Planner**: Creates design documents 
and architectural plans in `.agent_tasks/<task>/docs/`\n- **Explorer**: Stores 
research findings and analysis in `.agent_tasks/<task>/analysis/` and 
`.agent_tasks/<task>/docs/`\n- **All Agents**: Should follow this convention for
any non-source artifacts they create\n\n### Working Memory Management\n\nAgents 
maintain working memory to optimize performance and reduce redundant file 
reads:\n\n#### Working Memory Template\n```yaml\nworking_memory:\n  
current_task: "string describing active task"\n  task_objectives: ["specific", 
"goals", "for", "task"]\n  recent_files:\n    - path: "file/path.py"\n      
purpose: "why this file was read"\n      timestamp: "ISO timestamp"\n      
lines_read: "start_line-end_line or \'full\'"\n      key_insights: ["important",
"findings", "from", "file"]\n  active_context:\n    project_structure: "brief 
